{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-mass-energy","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:mass-energy","kind":"definition","title":"Energy of a braid class ($\\mathfrak{E} = \\mathfrak{m} \\cdot c_q^2$)","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-information-speed-of-light","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-mass-identity"],"tags":["mass-energy","speed-of-light","information-theory"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Information.energy","text":"mass-energy-equivalence.md","leanSource":"mass-energy-equivalence.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:mass-energy\"></a><p><em>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, \\varTheta, G, \\mathcal{S})</code> be an archimedean quantum observable universe with substrate parameter <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q > 1</code> and speed of light <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">c_q = 1/(q-1)</code> (<a href=\"#def:information-speed-of-light\" data-at=\"information-theory/speed-of-light\">speed of light</a>). Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{m}(\\beta)</code> be the mass of a braid class <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\beta</code> (<a href=\"#def:mass-identity\" data-at=\"mass-endomorphism/mass-endomorphism-opener/mass-endomorphism-mass-identity\">mass identity</a>). The <strong>energy</strong> of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\beta</code> is</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\mathfrak{E}(\\beta)\n  =  \\mathfrak{m}(\\beta) \\cdot c_q^2\n  =  \\frac{\\mathfrak{m}(\\beta)}{(q - 1)^2}.</code></pre>\n<p>The bare symbol <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{E}</code> denotes this energy. Other energies carry a subscript, for example the crossing energy <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{E}_{\\mathrm{cross}}</code> (<a href=\"#def:crossing-energy\" data-at=\"knots-particles-confinement/nucleon-derivation\">crossing energy</a>).</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/mass-energy-equivalence.md","heading":"Definition","number":"22.4.4","page":"b/def-mass-energy","qa":{"counts":{"pass":87,"fail":0,"warn":1,"na":12,"unknown":0,"stale":73},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.Information.energy","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/mass-energy-equivalence.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
